<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  fpv_quad_enemy -- a PROPER 3D quadcopter target, red "enemy" accented.

  WHY THIS MODEL EXISTS: models/fpv_target_markerless (and models/fpv_target,
  models/apriltag_target before it) lay their 4 arms/props out in the LOCAL
  Y-Z PLANE -- e.g. arm_ne_visual pose "0.14 -0.205061 0.205061 ...": fixed
  local X, varying Y/Z. Since local Z is up, that puts the rotor plane
  VERTICAL -- it is a flat billboard facing -X, not a real quad, and it reads
  as fake the moment the mover yaws/banks/pitches it (a horizontal quad's
  rotor disc should stay in the local X-Y plane). This model fixes that by
  using the REAL x500 airframe meshes (vendored below) so the rotor plane is
  genuinely HORIZONTAL and the silhouette is correct from every viewing
  angle, at every attitude the mover commands.

  LOCAL FRAME: FORWARD = +X (nose), rotor plane HORIZONTAL in X-Y, +Z up.
  Static, teleported by scripts/m4_target_mover.py (no physics, no joints).
  Red enemy accents on the 4 prop + 4 motor-bell visuals so it reads as a
  hostile target distinct from the (dark carbon / blue-accented) interceptor
  airframe -- see models/x500_base/model.config for that reskin's rationale.

  Forward-axis confirmation: PX4-Autopilot's x500_base/model.sdf places its
  NXP_FMUK66_FRONT decal visual at pose "0.047 .001 .043 ..." -- a positive-X
  offset -- i.e. the nose/front of the real x500 airframe is +X. This model
  keeps that convention so scripts/m4_target_mover.py's yaw-toward-heading
  logic (which assumes +X = forward) points the nose the right way.

  PROVENANCE: geometry, meshes, and material are copied/flattened from
  PX4-Autopilot's Tools/simulation/gz/models/x500_base/model.sdf (the real
  x500 quad used by the interceptor itself). This is a NEW model -- it does
  NOT touch models/fpv_target_markerless/ or any other existing target.

  STRUCTURE: ONE static link ("base") with ONLY <visual> elements -- no
  <collision>, no <inertial>, no <joint>, no <plugin>, no separate rotor
  links. x500_base's 4 rotors are each their own link (joined to base_link by
  a revolute joint) purely so PX4/Gazebo can spin the props; since this
  target is teleported kinematically and never spins props, every rotor's
  visuals are FLATTENED into "base" by composing the rotor link's pose with
  each visual's local pose (both are pure translations -- x500_base's rotor
  links and their visuals carry zero rotation relative to each other -- so
  the flatten is just vector addition; the visual's own mesh rotation, e.g.
  the frame mesh's 180 deg yaw, is preserved unchanged):

    rotor_0 link pose      (0.174, -0.174, 0.06)   [x500_base/model.sdf L316-320]
    rotor_0_visual pose  + (-0.022, -0.14638461538461536, -0.016)  [L329-330]
    ---------------------------------------------------------------
    flattened prop_0 pose   (0.152, -0.32038461538461536, 0.044)

    rotor_0_visual_motor_bell pose (0, 0, -0.032) added to the SAME rotor_0
    link pose (0.174, -0.174, 0.06) gives the flattened bell_0 pose
    (0.174, -0.174, 0.028).

  The base_link_visual (airframe) and 4 5010_motor_base_N visuals need no
  composition: in x500_base, base_link itself carries no <pose> (identity
  relative to the model root), so those visual poses are copied verbatim.

  Full per-rotor arithmetic (source: x500_base/model.sdf, this repo's copy
  at models/x500_base/model.sdf, read verbatim before writing this file):

    rotor_0: link (0.174, -0.174, 0.06), prop mesh 1345_prop_ccw.stl
      prop visual local  (-0.022, -0.14638461538461536, -0.016)
      -> flattened        (0.152, -0.32038461538461536, 0.044)
      bell visual local  (0, 0, -0.032)
      -> flattened        (0.174, -0.174, 0.028)

    rotor_1: link (-0.174, 0.174, 0.06), prop mesh 1345_prop_ccw.stl
      prop visual local  (-0.022, -0.14638461538461536, -0.016)
      -> flattened        (-0.196, 0.02761538461538464, 0.044)
      bell visual local  (0, 0, -0.032)
      -> flattened        (-0.174, 0.174, 0.028)

    rotor_2: link (0.174, 0.174, 0.06), prop mesh 1345_prop_cw.stl
      prop visual local  (-0.022, -0.14638461538461536, -0.016)
      -> flattened        (0.152, 0.02761538461538464, 0.044)
      bell visual local  (0, 0, -0.032)
      -> flattened        (0.174, 0.174, 0.028)

    rotor_3: link (-0.174, -0.174, 0.06), prop mesh 1345_prop_cw.stl
      prop visual local  (-0.022, -0.14638461538461536, -0.016)
      -> flattened        (-0.196, -0.32038461538461536, 0.044)
      bell visual local  (0, 0, -0.032)
      -> flattened        (-0.174, -0.174, 0.028)

  All flattened poses keep the visual's own rotation (0 0 0 for props and
  bells; the frame mesh keeps its 180 deg yaw). Rotor-plane visuals sit at
  local z ~ 0.028-0.044 -- HORIZONTAL, next to the airframe at z ~ 0.025-0.032
  -- confirming this is a real 3D quad, not a vertical billboard.

  MESHES: vendored (real files, not symlinks -- verified with `ls -lL` and
  `file`) into models/fpv_quad_enemy/meshes/ from this repo's models/x500_base
  copy (itself a symlink farm to PX4-Autopilot's x500_base) via `cp -L`:
  NXP-HGD-CF.dae (airframe), 5010Base.dae (motor base x4), 5010Bell.dae
  (motor bell x4), 1345_prop_ccw.stl / 1345_prop_cw.stl (props x4), plus
  CF.png (the airframe mesh's own carbon-fiber texture, referenced by
  NXP-HGD-CF.dae's <library_images><init_from>CF.png</init_from>, vendored
  alongside it so the texture resolves).

  VALIDATION STATUS: static-checked only (`gz sdf -k`). No live spawn / no
  sim boot performed for this deliverable -- see docs/decisions.md for the
  ADR covering this model's introduction.
-->
<sdf version='1.9'>
  <model name="fpv_quad_enemy">
    <static>true</static>
    <pose>0 0 0 0 0 0</pose>
    <link name="base">

      <!-- Airframe (carbon-fiber frame mesh). Copied verbatim from
           x500_base's base_link_visual -- no composition needed since
           base_link carries no pose relative to the x500_base model root. -->
      <visual name="frame_visual">
        <pose>0 0 .025 0 0 3.141592654</pose>
        <geometry>
          <mesh>
            <scale>1 1 1</scale>
            <uri>model://fpv_quad_enemy/meshes/NXP-HGD-CF.dae</uri>
          </mesh>
        </geometry>
      </visual>

      <!-- 4 motor bases (the arm-tip mounts the rotor bells sit on). Copied
           verbatim from x500_base's 4 5010_motor_base_N visuals. -->
      <visual name="motor_base_0">
        <pose>0.174 0.174 .032 0 0 -.45</pose>
        <geometry>
          <mesh>
            <scale>1 1 1</scale>
            <uri>model://fpv_quad_enemy/meshes/5010Base.dae</uri>
          </mesh>
        </geometry>
      </visual>
      <visual name="motor_base_1">
        <pose>-0.174 0.174 .032 0 0 -.45</pose>
        <geometry>
          <mesh>
            <scale>1 1 1</scale>
            <uri>model://fpv_quad_enemy/meshes/5010Base.dae</uri>
          </mesh>
        </geometry>
      </visual>
      <visual name="motor_base_2">
        <pose>0.174 -0.174 .032 0 0 -.45</pose>
        <geometry>
          <mesh>
            <scale>1 1 1</scale>
            <uri>model://fpv_quad_enemy/meshes/5010Base.dae</uri>
          </mesh>
        </geometry>
      </visual>
      <visual name="motor_base_3">
        <pose>-0.174 -0.174 .032 0 0 -.45</pose>
        <geometry>
          <mesh>
            <scale>1 1 1</scale>
            <uri>model://fpv_quad_enemy/meshes/5010Base.dae</uri>
          </mesh>
        </geometry>
      </visual>

      <!-- 4 props -- FLATTENED from x500_base's rotor_N link pose + that
           rotor's own *_visual local pose (see header derivation). RED enemy
           accent material (the ADR-0033-style "enemy" tint used elsewhere in
           this repo, e.g. fpv_target_markerless's hub visuals). -->
      <visual name="prop_0">
        <pose>0.152 -0.32038461538461536 0.044 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <mesh>
            <scale>0.8461538461538461 0.8461538461538461 0.8461538461538461</scale>
            <uri>model://fpv_quad_enemy/meshes/1345_prop_ccw.stl</uri>
          </mesh>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.5 0.03 0.03 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.8 0.05 0.05 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.3 0.1 0.1 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="prop_1">
        <pose>-0.196 0.02761538461538464 0.044 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <mesh>
            <scale>0.8461538461538461 0.8461538461538461 0.8461538461538461</scale>
            <uri>model://fpv_quad_enemy/meshes/1345_prop_ccw.stl</uri>
          </mesh>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.5 0.03 0.03 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.8 0.05 0.05 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.3 0.1 0.1 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="prop_2">
        <pose>0.152 0.02761538461538464 0.044 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <mesh>
            <scale>0.8461538461538461 0.8461538461538461 0.8461538461538461</scale>
            <uri>model://fpv_quad_enemy/meshes/1345_prop_cw.stl</uri>
          </mesh>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.5 0.03 0.03 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.8 0.05 0.05 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.3 0.1 0.1 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="prop_3">
        <pose>-0.196 -0.32038461538461536 0.044 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <mesh>
            <scale>0.8461538461538461 0.8461538461538461 0.8461538461538461</scale>
            <uri>model://fpv_quad_enemy/meshes/1345_prop_cw.stl</uri>
          </mesh>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.5 0.03 0.03 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.8 0.05 0.05 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.3 0.1 0.1 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>

      <!-- 4 motor bells -- FLATTENED from the same rotor_N link pose + that
           rotor's *_visual_motor_bell (x500_base rotor_0) / *_motor_top
           (rotor_1..3, same mesh) local pose (0,0,-0.032). RED enemy accent
           to match the props. -->
      <visual name="bell_0">
        <pose>0.174 -0.174 0.028 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <mesh>
            <scale>1 1 1</scale>
            <uri>model://fpv_quad_enemy/meshes/5010Bell.dae</uri>
          </mesh>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.5 0.03 0.03 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.8 0.05 0.05 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.3 0.1 0.1 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="bell_1">
        <pose>-0.174 0.174 0.028 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <mesh>
            <scale>1 1 1</scale>
            <uri>model://fpv_quad_enemy/meshes/5010Bell.dae</uri>
          </mesh>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.5 0.03 0.03 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.8 0.05 0.05 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.3 0.1 0.1 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="bell_2">
        <pose>0.174 0.174 0.028 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <mesh>
            <scale>1 1 1</scale>
            <uri>model://fpv_quad_enemy/meshes/5010Bell.dae</uri>
          </mesh>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.5 0.03 0.03 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.8 0.05 0.05 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.3 0.1 0.1 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="bell_3">
        <pose>-0.174 -0.174 0.028 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <mesh>
            <scale>1 1 1</scale>
            <uri>model://fpv_quad_enemy/meshes/5010Bell.dae</uri>
          </mesh>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.5 0.03 0.03 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.8 0.05 0.05 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.3 0.1 0.1 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>

    </link>
  </model>
</sdf>
